// MonitorInputSwitcher.cpp
// Ultra-lightweight monitor input switcher: DDC/CI (VCP 0x60) + floating desktop buttons.
// Pure Win32 / GDI, no external dependencies, no polling (idle = 0% CPU).
// Needs mis_icons.h (embedded icon set, generated by make_icons.py) next to this file.
//
// Build (MSVC, from a Developer Command Prompt):  see build.bat
//
// Usage
//   * Left-click a button          -> switch the configured monitor to the configured input
//   * Drag a button                -> move it (position is saved)
//   * Right-click a button         -> Configure / Add / Delete / Lock / Exit ...
//   * Tray icon                    -> left-click = show/hide buttons, right-click = menu
//
// Each button can show a label, an icon, or both (label above or below the icon). Icons are
// either one of the built-in set or any .ico file; icon opacity and button opacity are separate.
//
// The tray icon comes in a light (for dark taskbars) and a dark (for light taskbars) variant,
// chosen automatically from the Windows theme or fixed via the tray menu (Tray icon).
// Icons live in the resource file app.rc (app.ico, tray-light.ico, tray-dark.ico) - see build.bat.
//
// Settings are stored in MonitorInputSwitcher.ini next to the .exe (UTF-16, hand-editable).
//
// Command line (scripting / shortcuts / schedulers) - run with --help for the full list:
//   MonitorInputSwitcher.exe --monitor 1 --input hdmi1
//   MonitorInputSwitcher.exe 1=hdmi1 2=dp1
//   MonitorInputSwitcher.exe --button "HDMI"
// Build with -DMIS_CLI /SUBSYSTEM:CONSOLE for a console twin (mis-cli.exe) whose exit code
// batch files can read directly (the GUI exe needs "start /wait" for that).

